0:{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[[["$","$L2","it-2021",{"law":{"id":"it-2021","title":"Intermediary Guidelines and Digital Media Ethics Code Rules, 2021","short":"IT Rules, 2021","year":"2021 · amended in 2025 and 2026","kind":"Rule","status":"current","summary":"Intermediary due diligence, social-media duties, grievance redressal, digital-media ethics, and the newer synthetic-information framework.","url":"https://www.meity.gov.in/static/uploads/2026/03/0b576f2071694b52e4cd6bb1b6dfab1e.pdf","caution":"This study guide identifies the amended framework. Read G.S.R. 120(E), the 26 February 2026 corrigendum, and subsequent changes for the exact operative wording.","topics":["1.11","3.4","5.7"],"sections":[{"number":"1–2","title":"Scope and definitions","text":"Identify the regulated intermediaries, social-media categories, publishers, and defined terms. The 2026 amendment adds synthetic-information concepts; not every automated edit or text-only output is treated identically."},{"number":"3(1)(a)–(c)","title":"Publication, user information, and cooperation","text":"Covers publication of rules and policies, user-information duties, and specified cooperation or assistance. The 2026 amendment changes the periodic user-information frequency to at least once every three months."},{"number":"3(1)(d)","title":"Actual knowledge and removal","text":"Addresses removal or disabling following actual knowledge through the specified court or government route. The 2025 amendment added authorization and reasoning safeguards and a 24-hour window; the 2026 amendment reduced that window to three hours."},{"number":"3(1)(e)–(j)","title":"User respect, complaints, and records","text":"Addresses the remaining due-diligence duties, including specified cooperation, complaint handling, and retention under the applicable clauses. Do not apply the 3(1)(d) clock to every type of complaint."},{"number":"3(2)","title":"Specified complaint categories","text":"Includes special handling for specified unlawful or harmful content, with distinct conditions and timelines. Preserve evidence and protect victims while following the exact applicable process."},{"number":"3(3) · 2026","title":"Synthetically generated information","text":"Introduces due-diligence measures for covered synthetic audio, visual, or audio-visual information, including technical measures, declarations, verification, labels, and provenance-related requirements within the notified scope and exclusions."},{"number":"3(4)–(6) · amended framework","title":"Clarifications, directions, and specific directions","text":"Distinguish the inserted compliance mechanism for Ministry communications from the separate specific-direction and grievance provisions. Check the current numbering and text before citing a new obligation."},{"number":"4","title":"Significant social media intermediaries","text":"Adds duties for qualifying significant intermediaries, including specified personnel, reporting, and traceability-related provisions subject to their conditions. Synthetic-media verification duties must also be read where applicable."},{"number":"5–7","title":"SSMI threshold and due diligence","text":"Identify the notification and user-threshold framework and additional duties. A platform’s category affects which obligations apply."},{"number":"8–10","title":"Grievance and compliance mechanisms","text":"Addresses grievance handling and compliance under the applicable Part. Keep complaint records, decisions, notices, and escalation routes distinct from a court’s adjudication."},{"number":"Part III","title":"Digital media and curated-content ethics","text":"Establishes the digital-media ethics and grievance framework for covered publishers. It is not a single process identical to social-media intermediary due diligence."},{"number":"Part III · appendices","title":"Programme and age-classification provisions","text":"Read the relevant Code and classification provisions for the specific publisher and content. Apply the actual procedure, not a generic takedown assumption."},{"number":"2025 amendment","title":"G.S.R. 775(E)","text":"Introduced senior-officer authorization, legal basis, specificity, and periodic review safeguards for the specified removal mechanism. Effective 15 November 2025; read with the later 2026 changes."},{"number":"2026 amendment","title":"G.S.R. 120(E)","text":"Notified 10 February 2026, generally effective 20 February 2026. Adds synthetic-media duties and changes specified timelines. The final text differs from the consultation draft, including fixed-percentage label proposals."}]}}]],["$L3"],"$L4"]}],"isPartial":false,"staleTime":300,"varyParams":null,"buildId":"mMiCr23A_-Cpk0hZkfT7X"}
